WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.252
Missing security requirements leave teams without clear expectations for authentication, authorization, auditing, data protection, rate limits, approval workflows, or CUI handling.

2
00:00:12.252 --> 00:00:17.241
Threat modeling helps teams identify likely abuse paths before code is deployed.

3
00:00:17.241 --> 00:00:24.385
It is most useful when it covers trust boundaries, sensitive data flows, privileged actions, and failure modes.

4
00:00:24.385 --> 00:00:32.028
Unsafe business logic can allow attackers to bypass intended workflows even when individual endpoints operate as written.

5
00:00:32.028 --> 00:00:37.027
Sequence enforcement, approval checks, and state validation are design concerns.

6
00:00:37.027 --> 00:00:45.927
Architecture reviews help identify misplaced trust in internal networks, client-side controls, service integrations, or manual processes.

7
00:00:45.927 --> 00:00:50.796
CMMC-aligned systems need defensible decisions and traceable risk handling.

8
00:00:50.796 --> 00:00:54.648
Use threat modeling for critical workflows and trust boundaries.

9
00:00:54.648 --> 00:00:59.078
Integrate secure SDLC practices into design and development.

10
00:00:59.078 --> 00:01:03.997
Perform security architecture reviews for systems that handle or affect CUI.

11
00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:07.470
Selected CMMC mappings for this topic include RA.

